From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:15:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gridcraft-aros: keep the main task's startup directory lock
 for the C library

Problem: ABIv11 crt.library keeps chdir's saved directory in one base for
  all tasks of the process, records the lock of whichever task changes
  directory first, and restores it on the main task at exit. realpath()
  changes directory (posixc/realpath.c: open(".") and fchdir), so a worker
  thread that calls std::fs::canonicalize first makes the library unlock
  the main task's Workbench startup lock at exit, which Workbench startup
  then unlocks again (a double UnLock of freed memory).
Here: its font scan resolves every font folder with std::fs::canonicalize on its font-scan thread, at every start.
Rationale: chdir(".") on the main task before any worker starts records
  the main task's own lock and gives the library a replacement lock it
  owns; the directory does not change. The same change as the PdfCraft
  AROS port's patch 0011, which a probe confirmed (CRT kept the worker's
  lock without it, the main task's lock with it). Not reproduced as a
  crash in GridCraft; the code path is the reason.
Scope: the AROS GUI entry point; failure stops before any worker exists.
Upstream-status: local-only; candidate for the AROS frontend.
Verification: disk-based Workbench start and close in the port's evidence.
Removal: when the C library keeps the saved directory per task.
---
 apps/gridcraft-aros/src/main.rs | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apps/gridcraft-aros/src/main.rs b/apps/gridcraft-aros/src/main.rs
index d8c98d9bdc6f18cd63688d58cad5482b136dc8b9..1b8576037186971c54852479449b6dff55570d1b 100644
--- a/apps/gridcraft-aros/src/main.rs
+++ b/apps/gridcraft-aros/src/main.rs
@@ -177,6 +177,17 @@ fn save_prefs(app: &SheetApp) {
 }
 
 fn main() {
+    // ABIv11's C library keeps one saved directory for the whole process and
+    // restores it on the main task at exit. Whichever task changes directory
+    // first decides what is saved, and realpath() (std::fs::canonicalize)
+    // changes directory. If a worker does it first, the library later unlocks
+    // the main task's Workbench startup lock, which Workbench startup then
+    // unlocks again. chdir(".") here, before any worker, keeps the main task's
+    // own lock saved and gives the library a replacement it owns.
+    if let Err(error) = std::env::set_current_dir(".") {
+        eprintln!("gridcraft: cannot preserve the startup directory: {error}");
+        std::process::exit(1);
+    }
     install_logger();
     let options = match parse_args() {
         Ok(Some(o)) => o,
